{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "group-mission",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "1. FIRELINE Scientific Mission & Core Objective",
      "x": -250,
      "y": -460,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-mission-text",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# 🔥 FIRELINE Scientific Engine\n\n**Mission**: Transform decades of heterogeneous microgravity combustion data into an auditable evidence linkage engine.\n\n**Central Question**: Given an exploration mission profile ($g, P, X_{O_2}, u_\\infty$, fuel), what does NASA evidence verify (**SUPPORTED**), what is physically scaled (**INFERRED**), and where are empirical voids (**EVIDENCE GAP**)?",
      "x": -230,
      "y": -420,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 260
    },
    {
      "id": "node-home-file",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "FIRELINE-Home.md",
      "x": 150,
      "y": -420,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 260
    },
    {
      "id": "group-flex",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "2. FLEX (PSI-69) — Liquid Droplet Extinction & Cool Flames",
      "x": -1000,
      "y": -50,
      "width": 450,
      "height": 560,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-flex-file",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "01-Research/FLEX-Research-Notes.md",
      "x": -980,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 410,
      "height": 240
    },
    {
      "id": "node-flex-desc",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### FLEX Physical Boundaries\n* **Phase**: Liquid ($n$-heptane, $n$-octane, methanol)\n* **Geometry**: Spherical droplet ($d_0 \\approx 1.5\\text{--}5.0\\text{ mm}$)\n* **Flow**: Quiescent ($u_\\infty = 0\\text{ cm/s}$, pure spherical diffusion)\n* **Pressure**: $101.3\\text{ kPa}$ & sub-atmospheric inert dilution\n* **Verified Finding**: Hot radiative extinction at finite diameter $d_{ext} > 0$ followed by sustained cool-flame NTC burning\n* **Primary Citation**: Nayagam et al. (*Combust. Flame*, 2015)",
      "x": -980,
      "y": 250,
      "width": 410,
      "height": 240
    },
    {
      "id": "group-bass",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "3. BASS-II (PSI-25) — Solid Opposed Flow & Quenching",
      "x": -480,
      "y": -50,
      "width": 450,
      "height": 560,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-bass-file",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "01-Research/BASS-II-Research-Notes.md",
      "x": -460,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 410,
      "height": 240
    },
    {
      "id": "node-bass-desc",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### BASS-II Physical Boundaries\n* **Phase**: Solid thermoplastic (Cast PMMA rods & slabs)\n* **Geometry**: $6.35\\text{--}12.7\\text{ mm}$ rods (axial stagnation); $1.2\\text{ mm}$ flat slabs (opposed duct)\n* **Flow**: Flow envelope $0\\text{--}55\\text{ cm/s}$ (rods); $1\\text{--}25\\text{ cm/s}$ (slabs)\n* **Pressure**: $101.3\\text{ kPa}$ ambient ISS cabin\n* **Verified Finding**: Low-speed radiative quenching limit below $1.5\\text{ cm/s}$; aerodynamic blowoff up to $50\\text{ cm/s}$ on rods\n* **Primary Citation**: Olson & Ferkul (*Combust. Flame*, 2017; rods); secondary flat fuel studies",
      "x": -460,
      "y": 250,
      "width": 410,
      "height": 240
    },
    {
      "id": "group-saffire",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "4. Saffire-I (PSI-98) — Macro-Scale Spacecraft Fire",
      "x": 40,
      "y": -50,
      "width": 450,
      "height": 560,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-saffire-file",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "01-Research/Saffire-I-Research-Notes.md",
      "x": 60,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 410,
      "height": 240
    },
    {
      "id": "node-saffire-desc",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Saffire-I Physical Boundaries\n* **Phase**: Solid composite fabric (SIBAL: 75% cotton / 25% fiberglass)\n* **Geometry**: Full scale ($0.4\\text{ m} \\times 1.0\\text{ m} \\times 0.4\\text{ mm}$)\n* **Flow**: Forced concurrent flow ($20.0\\text{ cm/s}$)\n* **Pressure**: $101.3\\text{ kPa}$ ($14.7\\text{ psia}$, nominal Cygnus)\n* **Verified Finding**: Steady spread ($2.0\\text{--}2.5\\text{ mm/s}$); broad parabolic flame without buoyant necking; closed vehicle $\\Delta P \\approx 3.8\\text{ kPa}$ (derived thermal estimate)\n* **Primary Citation**: Urban et al. (*Combust. Flame*, 2019)",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 250,
      "width": 410,
      "height": 240
    },
    {
      "id": "group-cross",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "5. Cross-Investigation Analysis & Physical Boundaries",
      "x": -750,
      "y": 570,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 450,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "node-cross-file",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "01-Research/Cross-Investigation-Analysis.md",
      "x": -730,
      "y": 610,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 380
    },
    {
      "id": "node-cross-rules",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Inviolable Physical Compatibility Boundaries\n\n1. **Liquid != Solid Phase Separation**:\n   * Droplet evaporation kinetics (FLEX) must **never** directly support solid polymer questions.\n\n2. **Opposed != Concurrent Flow Regimes**:\n   * Upstream conductive spread (BASS-II) is physically distinct from downstream flame preheating (Saffire-I).\n\n3. **Thermal Thickness Regime Coupling**:\n   * In opposed flow, thin fabrics ($Bi \\ll 0.1$) scale as $V_f \\propto 1/\\tau$, while thick rods ($Bi > 1.0$) have thickness-independent spread.\n   * Concurrent spread (Saffire) does not follow $1/\\tau$ scaling due to downstream preheat length growth.",
      "x": -370,
      "y": 610,
      "width": 380,
      "height": 380
    },
    {
      "id": "group-sq",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "6. Unresolved Scientific Questions & Scaling Roadmap",
